12. The 722/372 Case Study: Mathematical Specification

12.1 Data Structure

The corpus consists of 722 manuscripts organized into 372 families. Of these, approximately 162 manuscripts list a formalized main result in Lean, while the remaining manuscripts are unformalized.OpenAI explicitly warns that unformalized results “could have issues.”

Definition 12.1 (Corpus Graph). Let G_{722} be the subgraph of G_{t₀} induced by the 372 families, with edges to prior literature (arXiv, MathSciNet) and Lean declarations.

12.2 Bimodal Validation Prior

Definition 12.2 (Bimodal Prior). Set initial validation states empirically:

V_i(t₀) = 1.0 for the 162 families with machine-checked Lean main results.

