14. The Central Proposition

Proposition 14.1 (Scientific Breakthrough Propagation). Let 𝒟 be a validated set of AI-generated mathematical discoveries introduced at time t₀ into a knowledge graph G_{t₀}. If the discoveries exhibit sufficiently high novelty, validation, formal fertility, and network connectivity, then their cumulative downstream impact produces a measurable deviation from the counterfactual trajectory:

ΔK(t) = K_𝒟(t) − K₀(t) > 0

where K_𝒟(t) is the observed production trajectory and K₀(t) is the k-hop masked synthetic control.

