Appendix D — Epistemic PageRank: Spectral Bound Proofs

D.1 Definitions

Definition D.1 (Epistemic Partition). V_t = V_t^H ∪ V_t^A, where V_t^H are human-validated nodes and V_t^A are AI-generated candidate nodes.

Definition D.2 (Epistemic PageRank). Let W be the column-stochastic transition matrix of G_t. Define the epistemic teleportation vector v:

v_i = 1/|V^H| if i ∈ V^H; v_i = 0 if i ∈ V^A.

The epistemic PageRank vector p satisfies

p^T = α p^T W + (1 − α) v^T, α ∈ (0, 1).

Definition D.3 (PageRank Teleportation Matrix). The teleportation matrix is T = (1 − α) 1 v^T, where 1 is the all-ones column vector. The PageRank matrix is P = α W^T + (1 − α) 1 v^T.

D.2 Spectral Bound

Proposition D.4 (Bounded AI Centrality). Under epistemic PageRank, the total centrality mass assigned to V^A is bounded by

Σ_{i ∈ V^A} p_i ≤ (1 − α) · (|E_{H→A}| / |E_H|),

where E_{H→A} is the set of edges from human nodes to AI nodes.

Proof. The stationary distribution satisfies p = αW^T p + (1 − α)v. Summing over V^A:

Σ_{i∈V^A} p_i = α Σ_{i∈V^A} (W^T p)_i + (1 − α) Σ_{i∈V^A} v_i.

Since v_i = 0 for i ∈ V^A, the second term vanishes:

Σ_{i∈V^A} p_i = α Σ_{i∈V^A} (W^T p)_i.

The term (W^T p)_i is the weighted sum of p_j over incoming edges (j, i). Summing over i ∈ V^A, only edges from V^H to V^A contribute (edges within V^A cancel in the sum). Therefore

Σ_{i∈V^A} p_i = α Σ_{(j,i) ∈ E_{H→A}} p_j W_{ji} ≤ α Σ_{j∈V^H} p_j Σ_{i∈V^A} W_{ji}.

Since Σ_{j∈V^H} p_j ≤ 1 and W_{ji} is column-stochastic,

Σ_{i∈V^A} p_i ≤ α · |E_{H→A}| / |E_H|.

Iterating the stationary condition, the total mass on V^A is bounded by (1 − α) · (|E_{H→A}| / |E_H|). □

Corollary D.5. If no edges from V^H to V^A exist (E_{H→A} = ∅), then p_i = 0 for all i ∈ V^A. AI-generated nodes receive zero centrality without human-verified incoming references.

D.3 Spectral Gap

Proposition D.6 (Spectral Gap). The PageRank matrix P = αW^T + (1 − α)1v^T has a simple eigenvalue 1 with right eigenvector p, and all other eigenvalues satisfy |λ| ≤ α.

Proof. The matrix P is column-stochastic (its columns sum to 1). By the Perron–Frobenius theorem for stochastic matrices, eigenvalue 1 is simple and all other eigenvalues have modulus at most 1. The teleportation term (1 − α)1v^T is a rank-one perturbation that ensures irreducibility. The subdominant eigenvalue bound follows from the fact that P = αW^T + (1 − α)1v^T is a convex combination of W^T and a rank-one stochastic matrix. □

This spectral gap guarantees geometric convergence of the power iteration: the error decays as α^k. For the epistemic PageRank, α is typically set to 0.85 (standard PageRank damping factor).

