Appendix L — Falsification Conditions and Pre-Registered Thresholds

L.1 Primary Falsification Conditions

The framework is falsified if:

1. SBPI has no predictive advantage over citation baselines in rank correlation.
2. The formal fertility measure F_i(t₀) is uncorrelated with actual downstream Lean adoption.
3. The epistemic teleportation fails to suppress AI echo chamber effects.
4. The k-hop masked synthetic control fails pre-treatment fit diagnostics.
5. The change-point detector produces false positives on placebo subfields.
6. The Shapley synergy estimate is indistinguishable from zero.

L.2 Quantitative Thresholds

· SBPI must outperform the citation baseline by ≥ 20% in rank correlation on held-out historical data.
· Fertility must predict future research generation with p < 0.05 after controls.
· Interdisciplinary propagation must add incremental predictive value in cross-validation.
· Results must replicate across at least three scientific domains.
· The change-point detector must maintain a false-positive rate below 5% on placebo fields.

L.3 Pre-Registration Protocol

The pre-registration must include:

· Classification protocol for the 372 families.
· Expert review criteria for novelty and quality.
· Matching to human-generated baselines (MSC code, team size, prior impact).
· Primary and secondary outcomes (SBPI, SRSI, citations, patents, formal verification rate).
· Time horizons (1, 3, 5, 10 years).
· Falsification thresholds as above.

Registration venue: OSF or Zenodo with timestamped DOI.

